Z||000000||Fiasco||05-11-2000||02:58 AM||||In another thread, some of you guys were talking about a hose from the air intake that went nowhere? Could someone elaborate?<BR>I have the pipe across the firewall on my '85 SE v6, but it connects to the rear of the filter on the EGR vac. reg. solenoid on the pass. side of the engine. Is this what you're talking about? Is this correct?<BR>What factory recall are you referring to?<BR>-Kinda puzzled, here.<BR>T.I.A.||||reg||5
Z||000001||GWMORGAN||05-11-2000||12:05 PM||||The pipe that runs along the fire wall and goes nowhere was once connected to the rear valve cover as a breather hose. After the recall, it was re-routed to the air inlet hose (next to trottle body). The person who performed the recall just didn't bother to remove the pipe, which now serves no useful purpose as it is. My GT now has that "pipe" sitting there doing nothing.<BR>Hope this helps in explaining.||||reg||1
Z||000002||triker||05-11-2000||01:16 PM||||The pipe you're asking about is the filtered air vent to the EGR solenoid and is hooked up properly.  The 'pipe to nowhere' is a little bigger, but in the same area.||||reg||1
